## SQ-HH-1555h | hops column stops at height 5: a 7th lattice stays empty (fresh column, bot H 10 blocks away)
> setblock 31074 -61 30054 minecraft:dirt
> fill 31074 -60 30055 31074 -53 30055 minecraft:stone
> setblock 31074 -60 30054 hearthandharvest:hops[age=4,facing=north]
> fill 31074 -59 30054 31074 -54 30054 vinery:grapevine_lattice[facing=north]
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3000
sleep 40
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
> zq count 31074 -60 30054 31074 -54 30054 hearthandharvest:hops
waitlog \[zq\] done 20
> execute if block 31074 -54 30054 vinery:grapevine_lattice
sleep 1
expect count hearthandharvest:hops: 6\b
expect Test passed
look count 6 (hops at -60 to -55), the top lattice at -54 still empty; a count of 1 now (a player is near) means the spread itself does not start

## SQ-WO-06r | sleeps in a storm by day (no timer), wakes after the storm (polled)
> time set noon
> setblock 30090 -60 30020 mysticaloaktree:wise_oak
> weather thunder 600
sleep 120
> zwo state 30090 -60 30020
waitlog \[zwo\] done 20
> data get block 30090 -60 30020 creativeworldgen_sleep_until
> weather clear 100000
repeat 24
sleep 5
> zwo state 30090 -60 30020
end
waitlog \[zwo\] done 20
> data get block 30090 -60 30020 creativeworldgen_sleep_until
sleep 1
expect \[zwo\] 30090 -60 30020 .*state=sleeping
expect \[zwo\] 30090 -60 30020 .*state=(none|blinking)
look the read before the clear: "Found no elements matching" = storm sleep (sleep_until 0), a number = it was a tired sleep that started before the sky darkened; first awake poll after the clear; a later sleeping poll with a sleep_until is a tired roll, not the storm

## SQ-HH-501d | diagnostic: theft with the default carry (1200 ticks); does the crow reach the nest late (TODO #68)
> fill 31107 -61 30087 31133 -47 30113 minecraft:glass hollow
> fill 31108 -60 30088 31132 -48 30112 minecraft:air
